    reg {
        name = "V0_VOFFSET";
        desc = "V0_VOFFSET is the Vertical Scaling Offset register. The vertical scaling offset is affected by two factors: pan-scan and the field offset when frames are repeated. When there is no field offset, vluma_offset is the lowest integer bit plus the fractional bits of offset_pan-scan; in YCbCr422 format vchroma_offset equals vluma_offset; in YCbCr420 format, vchroma_offset = scaling_chroma/2-0.25. When a field offset is needed (for example for a still frame or a repeated frame), assuming the bottom field is repeated, the vluma_offset and vchroma_offset configured for the top field are the same as in the no-offset case above, and the bottom field configuration must take the field offset into account. V0_VOFFSET (offset 0x08E0, total reset 0x0000_0000; PROVEN: Hi3535 data sheet, PDF page 1013, section 5.10).";
        field {
            name = "vluma_offset";
            desc = "Vertical luma offset, two's complement representation, (s,4,12) format.";
